// ============================================================
// DumperTest58.rc — G2 step 3, the CROSS-VERSION half of the Tier-1 UE5 branch.
//
// THE ROW. Genau's version detection tries, in order: (0) CrashReportClient.exe's version,
// (1) the game exe's PE VERSIONINFO, then a memory string scan for an engine tag. Every stock
// UE title answers at Tier 0, so the memory-scan branch was recorded as "unverifiable on this
// inventory". `DumperTest.rc` (UE 5.4) removed that blocker; this file adds a SECOND engine
// version so the row proves the Tier-1 PARSE, not one hard-coded answer.
//
// MEASURED BASELINE, before this file existed (2026-09-07):
//     DumperTest58.exe                 prod=5.8.2.0  Tier0 -> 508  needle=utf16 ['++UE5+Release-5.8']
//     DumperTest58-Win64-Shipping.exe  prod=5.8.2.0  Tier0 -> 508  needle=utf16 ['++UE5+Release-5.8']
//     2 binaries. 0 can actually produce a Tier-1 line.
// The needle was ALREADY there. The only thing missing was a reason to look for it.
//
// EXPECTED after this file, in scan-0.log:
//     DetectVersion: PE VERSIONINFO Product=1.8 File=1.8 — unrecognised
//     PE resource failed, falling back to memory string scan
//     Tier 1 (utf16) '++UE5+Release-5.8' -> 508
//
// ⭐ WHY 1.8 AND NOT 1.2. The 5.4 fixture reports 1.2 and this one reports 1.8, DELIBERATELY.
// Two Tier-1 hosts that disagree prove the dumper PARSED the needle; two that agree would also
// pass if it were echoing a constant. The trailing digit is a mnemonic for the engine minor and
// nothing reads it — the only hard requirement is that the major is neither 4 nor 5, or Tier 0
// would recognise it and the row would never reach the scan.
//
// ⚠ UE 5.8's UBT IS NOT UE 5.4's — CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED. The suppression moved out of
// UEBuildBinary.SetupBinaryLinkEnvironment into a new CompileResourceFiles(), and the test was
// rewritten from `CustomResourceFiles.Length == 0` (over compiled .res) to
// `!InputFiles.Any(x => x != PCLaunchResource)` (over source .rc). Same outcome for us: a module
// .rc makes the predicate false and the whole Default.rc2 branch is skipped. 5.8 additionally
// links Launch's PCLaunch.rc alongside ours — verified harmless, it carries no VERSIONINFO in
// either 5.4 or 5.8, so this file supplies the exe's ONLY version block.
//
// ⛔ DO NOT #include ANY ENGINE HEADER HERE. rc.exe is handed the Windows SDK include path and
// NOTHING ELSE. The 5.4 fixture opened with `#include "Windows/WindowsHWrapper.h"` and killed the
// whole build with `RC1015: cannot open include file` before a single .cpp was compiled. Every
// field below is a literal, so <windows.h> alone is enough.
//
// ⚠⚠ THREE WAYS THIS SILENTLY MEASURES NOTHING:
//  (a) ⛔ DO NOT tick "Include Crash Reporter" when packaging. The CrashReportClient.exe source
//      runs FIRST and WINS, so a package carrying it never reaches the PE-resource branch at all.
//      ⚠ Check for the .EXE, not the name: a clean package still stages a dozen
//      Saved/Config/**/CrashReportClient.ini files and a name glob calls that a false FAIL.
//  (b) The StringFileInfo below must stay free of any '++UE5+Release-' or '5.8' substring. That
//      block is the THIRD detection fallback, and an engine tag there passes the row for the
//      wrong reason.
//  (c) ⛔ The staged `<Config>\Windows\DumperTest58.exe` is UE's ~150 KB BOOTSTRAP STUB, not the
//      game — it still carries Default.rc2's 5.8.2.0 and reports Tier0 -> 508. Inject into
//      `DumperTest58\Binaries\Win64\DumperTest58*.exe`. See README.md § Traps.
// ============================================================

#include <windows.h>

VS_VERSION_INFO VERSIONINFO
 FILEVERSION 1,8,0,0
 PRODUCTVERSION 1,8,0,0
 FILEFLAGSMASK 0x3fL
#ifdef _DEBUG
 FILEFLAGS 0x1L
#else
 FILEFLAGS 0x0L
#endif
 FILEOS 0x40004L
 FILETYPE 0x1L
 FILESUBTYPE 0x0L
BEGIN
    BLOCK "StringFileInfo"
    BEGIN
        BLOCK "040904b0"
        BEGIN
            // ⚠ Deliberately free of any "++UE5+Release-" or "5.8" substring — see (b) above.
            VALUE "CompanyName",      "DumperTest58"
            VALUE "FileDescription",  "DumperTest58 cross-version verification fixture"
            VALUE "FileVersion",      "1.8.0.0"
            VALUE "InternalName",     "DumperTest58"
            VALUE "LegalCopyright",   ""
            VALUE "OriginalFilename", "DumperTest58.exe"
            VALUE "ProductName",      "DumperTest58"
            VALUE "ProductVersion",   "1.8.0.0"
        END
    END
    BLOCK "VarFileInfo"
    BEGIN
        VALUE "Translation", 0x409, 1200
    END
END
